{
  "version": 2,
  "description": "Per-tenant feature switches (spec C6). A Super Admin turns these on or off for a tenant in Manage Tenant; the list is stored in tenants.enabledFeatures. Groups follow the sidebar sections (shared/catalogue-access.json), and every sidebar item a tenant role can reach has a switch except Overview, Tickets, AI Assistant, Digital Twin, 2027 Horizon (all view:dashboard), My Tasks and Notification Prefs (view:profile). For users of that tenant the server removes every switched-off permission, and every permission on the same resource as a switched-off view:X (manage:X and the like), from what their role grants. A feature with a parent is off whenever its parent is off. \"screen:<view>\" entries switch one Security or Compliance screen (they share view:security / view:compliance): the sidebar hides a switched-off screen and the server refuses the routes it owns in the manifest. Read by backend/tenant_features.py and components/ManageTenantModal.tsx.",
